[44.622726, "o", "&& python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info &&…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick smoke test to confirm packages can be installed:\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip install --dry-run requests 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip install --dry-run requests 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚠ .gnomon/roles.toml [roles.verifier]: the completion reviewer is run read-only, so note is withheld from it during a review.\r\npip is fully working again.\r\n\r\n**What was"]
[44.622745, "o", " wrong:** The `pip` package code (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/`) had been deleted, but the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) was left behind. This caused `ensurepip` to think pip was already installed and skip re-extracting the wheel, while the `pip3` entry point script failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory, then re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which extracted the bundled wheel and restored pip to a working state.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=18 surface=e9a3788f4265\r\n"]
